From 6d76ec530deb9f5178c5905e1e484fe73da36a3a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 01:02:37 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(bedrock): use shared HTTP signaling for BDS connections

BDS 1.26.51.1 returns successful capability responses without JSON metadata.
The bundled transport rejects that response before posting the client offer.
Use ViaBedrock's HTTP signaling implementation so the proxy follows the same
native-compatible connection flow as direct clients.

Account-free HTTP offers also require a signed player identity. Wait for
one real Java LoginHello before opening that backend, then use the core
self-signed AuthData token and key for both SDP and game login. Preserve
normal proxy login validation and online-mode verification after the
backend handshake. Cancel the bounded wait on disconnect or malformed
input, and do not retain another packet queue. Online accounts and
RakNet keep their existing connection path.

EmbeddedChannel tests cover one-Hello consumption, deadline cancellation,
disconnect cleanup and rejection of unexpected input. Exact offline
BDS1.26.51.1 opens the self-signed transport while rejecting unsigned
SDP with numeric37; initialized proxy gameplay remains a separate gate.
